{"event":"A batch of soft goat's cheese sold at a hillside farm shop in the Vennick uplands was found to contain Salmonella after two customers fell ill, and the remaining stock was withdrawn.","sources":["Dr. Imelda Corrigan, Duskfield Regional Health Office epidemiologist","Tobias Farrenmere, shopkeeper at Hobbleby Farm Shop","Duskfield Environmental Health Inspection Report","Hobbleby Farm Shop Till and Stock Ledger","Marrick Dairy Cooperative Cold Store Temperature Logger","Keswin Reference Laboratory Test Certificate"],"core":{"text":"On Thursday 23 October, the Keswin Reference Laboratory confirmed Salmonella in goat's cheese batch GC-1016 sold at Hobbleby Farm Shop, leading to a withdrawal of the batch that afternoon.","source":"Keswin Reference Laboratory Test Certificate"},"facts":[{"text":"The cheese in batch GC-1016 was made at Marrick Dairy Cooperative on Thursday 16 October and packed in 200-gram wedges.","source":"Marrick Dairy Cooperative Cold Store Temperature Logger"},{"text":"Hobbleby Farm Shop received its delivery of batch GC-1016 on the morning of Monday 20 October.","source":"Hobbleby Farm Shop Till and Stock Ledger"},{"text":"Two customers from separate households reported gastrointestinal illness to the Duskfield Regional Health Office on Wednesday 22 October.","source":"Dr. Imelda Corrigan, Duskfield Regional Health Office epidemiologist"},{"text":"Both ill customers told Dr. Corrigan that they had bought goat's cheese from Hobbleby Farm Shop.","source":"Dr. Imelda Corrigan, Duskfield Regional Health Office epidemiologist"},{"text":"The cold store logger at Marrick Dairy Cooperative recorded a steady 3.5 degrees Celsius for batch GC-1016 from 16 October until collection.","source":"Marrick Dairy Cooperative Cold Store Temperature Logger"},{"text":"An environmental health officer collected four sealed wedges from the shop display on 22 October for laboratory testing.","source":"Duskfield Environmental Health Inspection Report"},{"text":"The inspection report notes that the shop's display chiller read 6 degrees Celsius at the time of the visit.","source":"Duskfield Environmental Health Inspection Report"},{"text":"The Keswin Reference Laboratory identified the isolate as Salmonella serotype Enteritidis.","source":"Keswin Reference Laboratory Test Certificate"},{"text":"The laboratory certificate lists all four submitted wedges as positive.","source":"Keswin Reference Laboratory Test Certificate"},{"text":"The shop ledger shows that batch GC-1016 was delivered in 3 crates of equal size.","source":"Hobbleby Farm Shop Till and Stock Ledger"},{"text":"Tobias Farrenmere removed the remaining wedges from the display and placed them in a labelled bin in the back room on Thursday afternoon.","source":"Tobias Farrenmere, shopkeeper at Hobbleby Farm Shop"},{"text":"Mr. Farrenmere says the shop had sold goat's cheese from this supplier for several years without complaint.","source":"Tobias Farrenmere, shopkeeper at Hobbleby Farm Shop"},{"text":"The inspection report records that the shop slices no cheese on the premises and sells only factory-sealed wedges.","source":"Duskfield Environmental Health Inspection Report"},{"text":"The cooperative's logger shows its cold store door was opened 14 times on 17 October.","source":"Marrick Dairy Cooperative Cold Store Temperature Logger"},{"text":"The Duskfield Regional Health Office issued a public notice about batch GC-1016 on Thursday evening.","source":"Dr. Imelda Corrigan, Duskfield Regional Health Office epidemiologist"}],"disputes":[{"kind":"count","about":"number of GC-1016 wedges sold by Hobbleby Farm Shop before withdrawal","claims":[{"text":"The stock ledger shows 46 wedges of batch GC-1016 were sold before the withdrawal.","source":"Hobbleby Farm Shop Till and Stock Ledger"},{"text":"Mr. Farrenmere recalls that 58 wedges of batch GC-1016 were sold before the withdrawal.","source":"Tobias Farrenmere, shopkeeper at Hobbleby Farm Shop"}]},{"kind":"measurement","about":"temperature of the shop display chiller during the inspection visit","claims":[{"text":"The inspection report records the shop display chiller at 6 degrees Celsius during the visit.","source":"Duskfield Environmental Health Inspection Report"},{"text":"Mr. Farrenmere states the display chiller read 4 degrees Celsius on its own dial during the inspection visit.","source":"Tobias Farrenmere, shopkeeper at Hobbleby Farm Shop"}]}],"names":["Vennick","Keswin Reference Laboratory","Hobbleby Farm Shop","Duskfield Regional Health Office","Marrick Dairy Cooperative","Duskfield Environmental Health Inspection Report","Hobbleby Farm Shop Till and Stock Ledger","Marrick Dairy Cooperative Cold Store Temperature Logger","Keswin Reference Laboratory Test Certificate"]}

